<Base title="Building — Matthew McMahon" description="Polarity, a life operating system. The Aegis, a sovereign smartwatch built from scratch.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Building</p>
    <h1>Tools I wish existed.</h1>
    <p>
      I don't like renting my life from other people's platforms. So I build. Two things are in motion.
    </p>

    <h2>Polarity</h2>
    <p>
      One system to run your life. Your money, your goals, your habits — turned into a game you're actually
      winning. Net worth is your light level; the work you do is your damage. Level up in the real world.
    </p>

    <h2>The Aegis</h2>
    <p>
      A sovereign smartwatch, built from scratch — my own firmware, my own rules, a tool that answers to me
      and not to Apple. It's a hobby build, documented in the open. The whole point is ownership: hardware
      you understand top to bottom.
    </p>

    <p style="color:var(--ink-faint)">Build logs and demos are coming here.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
